    questionText: "Imports can be both visible and invisible. Explain the term visible import and give one example of a visible import for Ireland.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"Explanation: 6 marks (3m + 3m) + Example: 4 marks","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "A visible import is when Irish people puchase a pysical good from a business in another county. Money leaves Ireland and goes to another country.", marks: 6, contextNote: "The scheme prints 6m (3m + 3m) against this explanation — three marks for the physical good bought from a business abroad and three for the money leaving Ireland — so an explanation that stops at the first half stops at three.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "anyN", verbatim: "The example of a visible import given: any one of the following", marks: null, contextNote: "The scheme prints 4 against the example list and asks for one example, so one worked example is the whole four.", openList: true, group: {"claimMax":1,"perOption":4,"options":["An Irish supermarket buying fruit from Spain.","Irish consumers buying wine fom and France.","An Irish department store buys clothes from America.","Irish consumers buying cars from the UK."]} },
    ],
