    id: "bus-2023-ol-s2-q5bi", topicId: "business-2-13", conceptId: "stock-control-defined",
    section: "2", questionRef: "2023 OL Section 2 Q5(B)(i)",
    stem: "SweetKing is an online pick ‘n’ mix store which was founded by Nathan Adams in June 2020. Nathan sources his stock from Ireland, Belgium, Spain, and the UK. He has since expanded his business into retail.",
    questionText: "Explain the term stock control.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"5m (3 + 2)","answer":null,"ofParts":null,"perPart":null}, totalMarks: 5,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Stock control means ensuring that the business has optimum stock. This means the right amount of stock, at the right time. A business should not have too much or too little stock.", marks: 5, contextNote: "The scheme prices this 3 + 2 but prints it as one continuous answer, so all of it is what you are being paid for: saying what optimum stock actually means is where the last marks are, not an optional extra. Stopping at \"optimum stock\" does not get you the five.", openList: true },
    ],
